Always implicitly instantiate std::string members in user code

libstdc++.a's explicit instantiations of basic_string<char> and
basic_string<wchar_t> do not include out-of-line copies of every
inline member (e.g. the C++11 move constructor). The extern template
declarations in basic_string.tcc suppress implicit instantiation in
user translation units, so whenever GCC declines to inline a call to
one of those members -- which reliably happens at -Os and -O0 -- the
program fails to link with undefined references such as:

  undefined reference to `std::__cxx11::basic_string<...>::
      basic_string(std::__cxx11::basic_string<...>&&)'

Upstream already disables these extern template declarations for
C++23 ("so C++23 code will implicitly instantiate std::string and
std::wstring as needed"). Take that same well-tested path for all
standards by disabling the class-level extern template declarations
entirely; the _M_replace_cold suppression and the non-member operator
declarations are kept. Members instantiate as COMDATs in each TU and
deduplicate at link time, so -O2 code is unaffected and -Os/-O0 code
becomes self-sufficient. This fixes w64devkit's own -Os-compiled
tools and end users compiling with -Os or -O0 alike.

--- a/libstdc++-v3/include/bits/basic_string.tcc
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/include/bits/basic_string.tcc
@@ -1037,7 +1037,7 @@
   // contains).
   // Suppress the explicit instantiation declarations for C++23, so C++23
   // code will implicitly instantiate std::string and std::wstring as needed.
-# if __cplusplus <= 202002L && _GLIBCXX_EXTERN_TEMPLATE > 0
+# if 0 /* w64devkit: always implicitly instantiate, as C++23 does above */
   extern template class basic_string<char>;
 # elif ! _GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI
   // Still need to prevent implicit instantiation of the COW empty rep,
@@ -1065,7 +1065,7 @@
     getline(basic_istream<char>&, string&);

 #ifdef _GLIBCXX_USE_WCHAR_T
-# if __cplusplus <= 202002L && _GLIBCXX_EXTERN_TEMPLATE > 0
+# if 0 /* w64devkit: always implicitly instantiate, as C++23 does above */
   extern template class basic_string<wchar_t>;
 # elif ! _GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI
   extern template basic_string<wchar_t>::size_type
